id: pm-7nqo6b
title: "pm stats default output is dominated by rows that carry no information: 7 of 17 type buckets are zero, the status split agents actually need is missing, and the row contract costs more than the data"
description: "Measured on the live 2429-item tracker: the default TOON output is 745 bytes, of which the row_contract block is 285 bytes (38 percent). by_type zero-fills every registered type, so 7 of 17 rows report 0 - Card, Changeset, Event, Meeting, TwinAsset, TwinFacility and VcsRef - registered by the bundled exemplar extensions (kanban-profile, digital-twin-exemplar, vcs-exemplar) and by builtins this workspace does not use. by_status zero-fills 3 of 6. Meanwhile the question an agent actually asks, how many items of each type are open versus closed, is not answerable from stats at all and needs a second command (pm aggregate --group-by type --completion). Reshaping the default to drop zero rows, fold the lifecycle split into by_type and drop the row contract yields 468 bytes, 37 percent smaller while strictly more informative. Zero-fill is currently documented as intentional in docs/COMMANDS.md, so this is a declared default change rather than a bug fix. Risk to manage: by_type moves from a flat count map to a lifecycle-bucketed shape, so any downstream reader treating by_type values as numbers breaks; the opt-in restore flag and a contracts-snapshot update in the same change are the mitigation."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[5]: agent-ux,context-efficiency,output-contracts,stats,token-budget
created_at: "2026-08-11T05:23:41.349Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-11T05:26:12.572Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "Default pm stats omits every by_type and by_status row whose count is zero and reports the omitted bucket count as a scalar so the information is not lost; by_type carries the lifecycle split per type (total plus open, in_progress, blocked, draft, closed, canceled, other) derived from the groupItemsByDimension primitive that already serves --by-assignee, with no second traversal of the item set; An explicit opt-in flag restores the zero-filled distribution for governance dashboards that need unused states visible; Default pm stats emits no row contract block, and the reshaped default is added to the token-budget-gate corpus with a declared ceiling so the saving is enforced rather than observed once; docs/COMMANDS.md drops the zero-fill-is-a-feature claim and the contracts snapshot, completion scripts and MCP surface are regenerated in the same change"
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: medium
confidence: high
